# ProductEditor – Visible Fallback When UI Is Invisible/Empty

When **Console shows NO errors**, the **page IS rendering** (divs visible in Elements), but the **UI looks invisible or empty**, the problem is likely one of:

1. Product content is empty/null  
2. CSS is hiding everything  
3. Component is stuck in a "restoring" or conditional state  

## QUICK FIX: Add visible fallback content

**Target:** `ProductEditor.tsx` – find the **return** that renders the main editor (after loading and `!product` checks) and **temporarily** replace it with this debug view:

```typescript
return (
  <div className="min-h-screen bg-red-500 p-8 text-white">
    <h1 className="text-4xl mb-4">DEBUG VIEW</h1>
    <p>Product ID: {productId}</p>
    <p>Product loaded: {product ? 'YES' : 'NO'}</p>
    <p>Product title: {product?.title}</p>

    <div className="mt-8 bg-white text-black p-4">
      <h2 className="text-2xl mb-4">Product Content:</h2>
      <div dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: product?.content || 'NO CONTENT' }} />
    </div>
  </div>
)
```

**Notes:**

- Use the same `productId` and `product` (and any other names) as in the existing component (e.g. if the component uses `product` from state, keep that).
- If the editor returns `<ProductEditorContext.Provider>…<ProductEditorView /></ProductEditorContext.Provider>`, replace that **entire** return (for the success path only) with the debug div above so the red view is what the user sees.
- This is **temporary** – only to confirm render and data; revert once the cause is known.

## What this does

- **Bright red background** → confirms the component is rendering and not hidden by CSS.
- **Product ID / loaded / title** → confirms product data is present.
- **Product content block** → shows whether `product.content` (or equivalent) has HTML or is empty.

If you see the red screen with text:

- Rendering works.
- The issue is in the **complex UI** (e.g. ProductEditorView or nested components), not in data loading for this page.

## After adding

- Save the file, refresh the browser.
- **Screenshot** what you see (red view with or without content).
- Use that to decide: fix the real UI vs fix data/content. Then remove this debug return and restore the proper editor UI.
